+# BlockInfo performance report
+
+Script: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/BlockInfo.client.luau` (block counts panel and
+hover highlight).
+
+## Symptom
+
+With about 6,000 blocks placed, the client MicroProfiler showed `Script_BlockInfo` at about 2.5 ms
+every frame, usually followed by a GC label. A phone ran the same build at about 35 FPS. An empty
+baseplate was fine on both.
+
+## What was costing time
+
+All of the work ran in `RenderStepped`, so it ran every frame and held up rendering until it
+finished. Most of it grew with the number of blocks (N):
+
+| Per frame | Cost |
+|---|---|
+| `blocksFolder:GetChildren()` called **3 times** (counting, hover search, total) | Each call builds a new N-element array: three 6,000-entry tables per frame, which is what drove the GC label after the script |
+| Counting loop over every child | O(N) Luau work and a property read (`Name`) on every block |
+| Hover search: `IsA` + `.Position` + distance on every block | O(N) Instance property reads, the most expensive part per item |
+| `RaycastParams.new()` + a new filter table | More garbage every frame |
+| Panel text rebuilt with repeated `..` and assigned to `countsLabel.Text` | New strings every frame, and setting `Text` makes the engine redo text layout, even when nothing changed |
+| `selectionBox.Adornee` assigned every frame | Engine property write even when the hovered block hadn't changed |
+
+So the cost climbed in a straight line with build size and also made garbage in proportion to it.
+That explains why 6,000 blocks was already a problem and larger builds would be worse.
+
+## What changed
+
+What players see is the same: same panel layout, same text, same counts (including `Total`
+counting every child of `Blocks`), and the same "nearest block center within `HOVER_RADIUS` of
+the point under the mouse" hover rule.
+
+1. **Counts are tracked incrementally.** `ChildAdded` / `ChildRemoved` on `Workspace.Blocks`
+   update per-type counts and a total. Existing children are counted once at startup. The frame
+   loop no longer touches the folder's children.
+2. **Hover uses a spatial hash.** Each block is filed under its `BLOCK_SIZE` grid cell
+   (`floor(position / 4)`) when it's added and removed from it when it goes away. Since
+   `HOVER_RADIUS <= BLOCK_SIZE`, any block center close enough to count has to sit in the hit
+   point's cell or one of its 26 neighbours. So each frame checks at most 27 cells (in practice a
+   handful of blocks) instead of all N, and the exact distance test and nearest-wins rule are
+   unchanged.
+3. **One `RaycastParams` is reused.** Its filter is rebuilt only when `LocalPlayer.Character`
+   changes.
+4. **The panel only updates when something changed.** The text is rebuilt with `table.concat`
+   into a reused buffer, only when a count or the hovered block changes. `Adornee` is only written
+   when the hovered block changes.
+
+What's left per frame is one raycast, up to 27 hash lookups, and two comparisons, no matter how
+big the build is. No per-frame allocations grow with N.
+
+### Assumptions (true for the current server code)
+
+- Blocks don't move after they're placed. `BlockPlacement.server.luau` places anchored parts
+  and never moves them. If blocks ever become movable, the spatial hash has to re-file a block
+  when its `Position` changes.
+- Blocks aren't renamed after they're placed. The server sets `Name` before parenting. If
+  renaming is ever added, the counts have to listen for `Name` changes.
+- `HOVER_RADIUS` must stay `<= BlockTypes.BlockSize`. If it's raised, widen the neighbour search
+  from ±1 to ±`ceil(HOVER_RADIUS / BLOCK_SIZE)` cells.
+
+## What to check in Studio
+
+1. **MicroProfiler, same ~6,000-block build** (Ctrl+F6 on the client, then pause and look at a
+   few frames): `Script_BlockInfo` should be in the tens of microseconds and flat. The GC label
+   that used to follow it should be gone or much rarer.
+2. **Scaling:** build (or script-place) 20k–50k blocks and confirm `Script_BlockInfo` costs about
+   the same as at 6k. Note that joining a server with a huge build triggers one burst of
+   `ChildAdded` events. That's a one-time spike, not a per-frame cost.
+3. **Phone:** the 6,000-block build should be back to its empty-baseplate frame rate (check with
+   the Ctrl+Shift+F5 stats, or the Developer Console's MicroProfiler on device). If FPS is still
+   low but `Script_BlockInfo` is cheap, the remaining cost is rendering the parts themselves, not
+   this script.
+4. **Behaviour stays the same:**
+   - Place and delete blocks of each type: per-type counts and `Total` update right away.
+   - Hover over block tops, sides, edges and corners, and over the baseplate right next to a block
+     (the old rule highlighted a block whose center is within 4 studs, and the new one still
+     does). The highlight and "Pointing at:" should match what they did before.
+   - Reset your character and confirm the raycast still ignores it (hovering through your own
+     avatar should still find blocks).
+   - With StreamingEnabled, walk far away and back. Counts follow what's streamed in, as they did
+     before, since both versions only see blocks present on the client.
